// Reading the input.
//
// The document is copied into the flat store at xml_open and read from there
// with peek8, never with charat over the string.
//
// charat's bounds check is memoised on the *last* string it was asked about.
// A scanner that reads the document, builds a piece of a run out of it, and
// then reads the document again switches that memo twice per run and pays a
// full strlen of the whole input each time. Measured on a 14 MB content.xml:
// 1.76 s that way, and linear-with-a-small-constant through the store. peek8
// is bounds-checked against the store's high-water mark and costs the same for
// every byte, whatever was read last.

// The address of the input in the flat store.
xml_base() {
} return word (import xml_mem)[0];

// The length of the input, measured once at xml_open and kept. len(s) is a
// strlen every time it is evaluated and is not memoised, so a scanner that
// asks for it per attribute is scanning the whole document per attribute.
xml_len() {
} return int (import xml_st)[6];

// One byte of the input, or -1 at either end -- the same contract charat has,
// so that a scan can detect its own end without a separate bound. peek8 traps
// outside the store rather than answering, so the bound is checked here.
xml_ch(int i) {
  int c = -1;
  if(i >= 0 && i < xml_len()) {
    c = peek8(xml_base() + i);
  }
} return int c;
